		{"id":"58646d7ffaf7ba16","x":0,"y":40,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"Field theory 域论\n\nA map of field theory, from polynomials to Galois groups. It reads from left to right: a grey arrow from the right side of a card leads to the left side of a card that builds on it. A green line leads down to an example or a detail, and a purple line joins two related topics.\n\n- ⌘/Ctrl + wheel zooms. Alt + wheel spreads the cards, so each card shows more of its note.\n- A link such as [[Galois group]] moves the view to its card.\n- Press a card, then In or Out in its corner, to see the cards to read before or after it."},
