		{"id":"c0c42fa8af70e602","x":4820,"y":2160,"width":400,"height":240,"type":"text","text":"Running example: $E = \\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{2}, \\sqrt{3})$\n\n- $[E : \\mathbb{Q}] = 4$, with basis $1, \\sqrt{2}, \\sqrt{3}, \\sqrt{6}$\n- $E = \\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{3})$, and $\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{3}$ has minimal polynomial $x^4 - 10x^2 + 1$\n- $\\operatorname{Gal}(E/\\mathbb{Q}) = \\{1, f, g, fg\\}$, the Klein four-group\n- five subgroups, matching five intermediate fields","color":"4"}
	],
